# Characters that start no token.
mode: syntax
---- query
t | where x > 1 # comment?
| extend y = `z`
---- expected
IDENT@0..1 "t"
WHITESPACE@1..2 " "
PIPE@2..3 "|"
WHITESPACE@3..4 " "
IDENT@4..9 "where"
WHITESPACE@9..10 " "
IDENT@10..11 "x"
WHITESPACE@11..12 " "
GT@12..13 ">"
WHITESPACE@13..14 " "
LONG@14..15 "1"
WHITESPACE@15..16 " "
ERROR@16..17 "#"
WHITESPACE@17..18 " "
IDENT@18..25 "comment"
ERROR@25..26 "?"
WHITESPACE@26..27 "\n"
PIPE@27..28 "|"
WHITESPACE@28..29 " "
IDENT@29..35 "extend"
WHITESPACE@35..36 " "
IDENT@36..37 "y"
WHITESPACE@37..38 " "
EQ@38..39 "="
WHITESPACE@39..40 " "
ERROR@40..43 "`z`"
WHITESPACE@43..44 "\n"

error[DS0001]: unexpected character `#`
  --> query:1:17
  |
1 | t | where x > 1 # comment?
  |                 ^ not valid here
  |
  = help: comments start with `//`

error[DS0001]: unexpected character `?`
  --> query:1:26
  |
1 | t | where x > 1 # comment?
  |                          ^ not valid here
  |
  = help: for a conditional value, use `iff(condition, then, else)`

error[DS0001]: names are not quoted with backticks
  --> query:2:14
  |
2 | | extend y = `z`
  |              ^^^ backticks are not a quote
  |
  = help: quote the name with brackets: `['z']`
